cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mcfcg: column generation for minimum-cost multicommodity flow"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software (this file) and the
  accompanying paper (listed under preferred-citation).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Spoorendonk
    given-names: Simon
    email: simon@flowty.ai
    affiliation: Flowty ApS
  - family-names: Petersen
    given-names: Bjørn
    email: bjorn@flowty.ai
    affiliation: Flowty ApS
repository-code: "https://github.com/spoorendonk/mcfcg"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-11
abstract: >-
  A column generation solver for the minimum-cost multicommodity flow problem,
  supporting both path-based and tree-based Dantzig-Wolfe decompositions over a
  shared CG loop. Includes four LP backends (HiGHS, MOSEK, COPT, NVIDIA cuOpt)
  behind one interface, the instance-preparation and benchmark scripts, and the
  result tables reported in the accompanying paper. PROVENANCE.txt pins the
  exact solver versions and host behind those tables.
keywords:
  - multicommodity flow
  - column generation
  - Dantzig-Wolfe decomposition
  - linear programming
  - operations research
